      "writtenOn": "2026-09-21T12:48:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Awaitility\u0027s untilAsserted only retries on AssertionError - any other throwable, including the checked ExecutionException and InterruptedException from future.get(), is rethrown as-is through a sneaky-throw, so these signatures now understate what callers can receive and a caller can no longer write catch (ExecutionException e) around them. Could the poll body convert a read failure into an AssertionError so it is retried, and the throws clauses be kept where an exception really can escape?",
      "revId": "febc9de080c2ade0848082c16fc7322ef7b57cd0",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
